  "query_preview": "..\nVisible satellite imagery shows a departing weak trade-wind trough \nthat mildly disrupted the dry background trade-wind regime today. \nStarting tonight, low-end (10%) isolated showers and light to gentle\neast winds will return for the Marianas through Saturday, becoming \n20 percent PoPs until the latter half of the week. Forecaster \nconfidence is extremely low regarding the timing, intensity, and \ntrack of Invest 92W (see Tropical Systems section below) as the \ndifferent model groups disagree from each other. Therefore, PoPs \nwere kept at 30 percent for the last few periods of the forecast. \nWhether or not this system impacts the Marianas will greatly depend \non its evolution for the next several days. Invest 92W will continue \nto be monitored and communicated.",
